meta {
  name: topics
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/topics
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  course_id: 1
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

docs {
  # GET /topics
  
  Retrieves topic modules for a course.
  
  ## HTTP Method & Route
  - **Method:** `GET`
  - **Route:** `/wp-json/tutor/v1/topics`
  
  ## Authentication
  - **With Bearer JWT:** user must be able to view the course (enrolled / instructor / public).
  - **Without JWT:** allowed only when the course is **public**.
  - Permission for JWT callers comes from the bound API key (`Read`, `Read/Write`, or `All`).
  
  ## Query Parameters
  
  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `course_id` | `integer` | **Yes** | Parent course post ID. Registered as a required REST arg; omitting it typically yields WordPress `rest_missing_callback_param` before the controller runs. |
  
  ## Notes — outline vs full DTO
  
  - **Full:** when the caller may reveal learning payloads (enrolled / instructor / public free course), each topic is a public post DTO: `ID`, `post_title`, `post_content`, `post_name`.
  - **Outline:** otherwise topics are outline-only: `ID`, `post_title`, `post_name` (no `post_content`).
  
  ## Responses
  
  ### 200 OK — full topic bodies
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_topic",
    "message": "Topic retrieved successfully",
    "data": [
      {
        "ID": 201,
        "post_title": "Getting Started with the Environment",
        "post_content": "Detailed overview of tools, IDE plugins, and prerequisites.",
        "post_name": "getting-started-environment"
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
  
  ### Missing `course_id` (WordPress validation)
  ```json
  {
    "code": "rest_missing_callback_param",
    "message": "Missing parameter(s): course_id",
    "data": {
      "status": 400,
      "params": ["course_id"]
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ### No topics
  ```json
  {
    "code": "tutor_read_topic",
    "message": "Topic not found for given course ID",
    "data": {
      "status": 404
    }
  }
  ```
}
